---
import Education from '../../layouts/Education.astro';
import TeachingDownloads from '../../components/TeachingDownloads.astro';
import {seminarSessions,rubric} from '../../data/education-kit.mjs';
import {educationModels} from '../../data/education-sources.mjs';
import {COURSE_CHAPTER_IDS} from '../../lib/course-criteria';
import {url} from '../../lib/site';
---
<Education title="Make room for a systems question." description="Start with an instructor-hosted lesson, adapt a seminar or develop a faculty-owned course through the university’s own process." filePath="src/pages/learn/universities.astro" active="universities" sourceIds={['mason-course-process','mason-cecil-faculty','philanthropy-lab-model','learning-by-giving-contact-model','campus-compact-faculty']}>
  <a slot="actions" class="btn" href="#seminar">Explore the sample seminar</a><a slot="actions" class="btn btn-ghost" href={url('/learn/teach/')}>Try one lesson</a>
  <section><h2>Choose the route with the host.</h2><div class="education-grid"><article class="education-card"><p class="eyebrow">An existing class</p><h3>Offer one inspectable activity.</h3><p>An instructor in ethics, economics, public policy, nonprofit studies or another relevant field can judge whether the <a href={url('/learn/teach/')}>50-minute case</a> fits. Offer goals, readings, a worksheet and worked notes, then ask what guest-speaker or teaching approvals apply. This is our proposed starting route, not a documented shortcut to permission.</p></article><article class="education-card"><p class="eyebrow">A new or changed course</p><h3>Find a faculty owner.</h3><p>A willing instructor and department can assess curricular fit, workload, assessment and the applicable approval route. As one local example, <a href="https://chss.gmu.edu/curriculum/submission_process">Mason CHSS describes department, college and university review</a>. The process and any general-education designation remain institutional decisions.</p></article></div><p>A student-led reading group is another option: use the <a href={url('/learn/clubs/')}>club guide</a> and current campus guidance. A syllabus download, guest session or self-study completion record does not create course credit or a recognized chapter.</p></section>
  <section id="seminar"><p class="eyebrow">Sample syllabus · untested teaching draft</p><h2>Eight meetings, ten chapters.</h2><p>This proposed seminar pairs chapters in two meetings and leaves the existing ten-unit course intact. The suggested format is eight 90-minute meetings. A host sets the actual contact time, prerequisites, reading load, access arrangements and assessment; no credit value is assigned here.</p><TeachingDownloads ids={['university-syllabus','complete-pack']} />{seminarSessions.map(session=><article class="education-session"><p class="eyebrow">Meeting {session.number}</p><h3>{session.title}</h3><p><strong>Reading:</strong> {session.chapters.map((chapter,index)=><>{index>0?' · ':''}<a href={url(`/record/principles/${COURSE_CHAPTER_IDS[chapter-1]}/`)}>Chapter {chapter}</a></>)}</p><p><strong>Exercise.</strong> {session.exercise}</p><p><strong>Reviewable output.</strong> {session.output}</p></article>)}</section>
  <section><h2>A capstone that assesses reasoning.</h2><p>Ask for a short fictional decision brief: a choice and alternative, causal map, costs and missing costs, observations versus assumptions, two moral perspectives, a feedback plan and a revision after peer challenge. Accept an equivalent diagrammatic or spoken response.</p><p>The proposed feedback rubric can be used without points, or with 0–3 per criterion, up to {rubric.length*3}. It is not a credential or a validated measure of professional competence. Do not reward a chosen cause, a higher depth number, agreement with the facilitator, donating or personal disclosure.</p><div class="education-table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Sample feedback rubric, scroll horizontally if needed" tabindex="0"><table class="education-table"><caption>Proposed classroom feedback rubric</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Criterion</th>{['0 · Missing','1 · Emerging','2 · Clear','3 · Well supported'].map(label=><th scope="col">{label}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>{rubric.map(row=><tr><th scope="row">{row.criterion}</th>{row.levels.map(level=><td>{level}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
  <section id="existing-models"><p class="eyebrow">Learn from existing practice</p><h2>Philanthropy education already exists.</h2><p>These official-source examples offer different models. Charitology is not a partner or a substitute for their programs. Our teaching pack uses fictional decisions and supplies no grant budget.</p><div class="education-grid">{educationModels.map(model=><article class="education-card"><p class="eyebrow">{model.format}</p><h3><a href={model.url}>{model.name}</a></h3><p>{model.description}</p><p class="education-limit">{model.limits}</p></article>)}</div></section>
</Education>
